# Qwen3.6-27B-FP8 — DENSE hybrid (GatedDeltaNet linear-attn + full-attn + dense SwiGLU), fp8, VL.
# Optimized serve, sized to CO-RESIDE with GLM-5.2 (fits the ~15GB/card GLM leaves free). TP=8.
# =================================================================================================
# ARCH (config + weight-index verified): 64 layers = 48 linear_attention (GatedDeltaNet SSM) + 16
#   full_attention (every 4th). DENSE SwiGLU MLP (gate/up/down_proj) — ZERO experts → NO expert-
#   parallel, NO routed-K, NO MoE fragmentation (the best-case Gaudi shape). fp8 block-quant
#   (weight + weight_scale_inv, e4m3 dynamic-activation). Vision tower MANDATORY (language_model_only
#   =False) — loads on HPU, we serve text (no images sent). Mamba/GDN params stay bf16 (checkpoint
#   ignore-list) — REQUIRED (quantizing the SSM path is what NaN-parked the 397B; do NOT force fp8 there).
#
# WHY THIS IS ~ZERO-BUILD (3-agent survey): vllm-gaudi (v0.20.1) REGISTERS Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration
#   in the hybrid allowlist — NO custom model class (unlike M3/GLM). Native HPU kernels exist for the
#   whole stack: HPUGatedDeltaNetAttention + hpu_gdn_pytorch (chunk_gated_delta_rule, recurrent update),
#   HPUMambaMixer2 + compiled mamba_pscan TPC kernels, hybrid conv/ssm+KV dual-cache, HPU vision graph.
#   fp8-KV proven 100%-accuracy on Qwen; serving recipe = the 397B-hybrid pattern (lazy + TP=8 +
#   per-layer mark_step). So this is CONFIG, not a build.
#
# OPTIMIZED LEVERS (all proven, just flipped on):
#   * TP=8 + lazy (PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE=1) + LAZY_COLLECTIVES: graphs the 8-way all-reduce (collective
#     penalty paid once at capture, not per token) — the 397B-sslazy8 win.
#   * --kv-cache-dtype fp8_inc: fp8 KV on the 16 full-attn (GQA) layers (linear-attn uses SSM state,
#     untouched/bf16). Proven 100% accuracy on Qwen3.6-35B.
#   * PER-LAYER mark_step LEFT DEFAULT (interval=1): LOAD-BEARING for GatedDeltaNet SSM-state
#     scheduling — 397B TEST: VLLM_CONFIG_HIDDEN_LAYERS=60 (coalesce) REGRESSED SS 28→6.4. Do NOT set it.
#   * --quantization fp8 (official quant_method) — vllm-gaudi fp8 path; dense SwiGLU uses STOCK ops
#     (NOT the M3 swigluoai monolithic — wrong activation → corruption; do not enable those).
#
# CO-RESIDENCE SIZING: GLM holds ~83GB/card, ~15GB free. Qwen fp8 weights ~4GB/card + graph + small KV
#   → util 0.12 (~11.5GB target) fits with margin. For a SOLO clean-validation run (cards free), raise
#   --gpu-memory-utilization to 0.85 for a full KV pool + true numbers.
#
# BRING-UP GATE (do first): coherence greedy (Paris/144/primes) — watch for NaN/garbage from the
#   fp8↔bf16-Mamba boundary (the 397B lesson; the bf16-Mamba checkpoint should clear it). Then SS c1 +
#   a c8 point. MTP is available (native head) but a SEPARATE arm — enable via --speculative-config
#   after the base serve is validated (it forfeits --async-scheduling).
# =================================================================================================
IMAGE=vllm-gaudi:next
MODEL_PATH=Qwen3.6-27B-FP8
SERVED_NAME=qwen36-27b
# EAGER (PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE=0) — the PROVEN Qwen3.6 path (qwen36.env/qwen3-30b use it). LAZY (=1) fails
# the hybrid+fp8+vision warmup graph compile (synStatus 26 in HabanaFusedOpLazy warmup_graphs). Under
# eager, torch.compile handles the GDN/Mamba+fp8+vision ops; no lazy fused-op recipe to choke on.
# VLLM_SKIP_WARMUP=true: skip the batch warmup graph-capture — under eager that spikes to the WHOLE
# card transiently (blocks co-residence). Skipping = ~13GB throughout; first request compiles on-demand.
MODEL_ENV="-e PT_HPU_LAZY_MODE=0 -e PT_HPU_WEIGHT_SHARING=0 -e VLLM_SKIP_WARMUP=true -e VLLM_ENGINE_ITERATION_TIMEOUT_S=1800 -e VLLM_RPC_TIMEOUT=100000000 -e VLLM_EXECUTE_MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600 -e VLLM_DECODE_BS_BUCKET_MIN=1 -e VLLM_GRAPH_RESERVED_MEM=0.10 -e VLLM_HPU_LOG_STEP_CPU_FALLBACKS=true"
# LEAN KV default (util 0.12 ~11.5GB/card, fp8_inc, ml 2048) — co-residence-ready, small footprint.
# One-off SOLO validation on free cards can raise --gpu-memory-utilization to 0.85 for a fat pool
# (throughput is pool-size-independent, so lean gives the same SS/conc numbers).
# MEMORY (measured): ~14GB/card = ~3.7GB sharded weights (31GB/8, correct) + ~9.4GB hybrid Mamba/GDN
# state pool + ~1GB overhead. The Mamba state pool is UTIL-SIZED, not seq-sized (max-num-seqs 8 vs 32 =
# same ~14GB, same 1.2M state blocks) -> max-num-seqs is FREE concurrency (crank it), and the real lean
# lever is --gpu-memory-utilization (0.12 -> lower shrinks the pool). fp8-KV barely matters (attn KV
# ~0.3%; the Mamba state dominates). 14GB co-resides fine under GLM (GLM ~50 + Qwen 14 = 64 of 96).
# KV = fp8_inc (the ONLY KV dtype vllm-gaudi supports = max compression; TurboQuant int4-KV is gated/
# uncompiled AND moot here — attn KV ~0.3%, the Mamba state pool is the footprint, sized by util).
# 2026-07-01 on-card: max-num-seqs 16->64 = FREE concurrency (util-sized pool, SAME 7.3GB). At util 0.04
# the lean pool MATCHES a 46GB fat pool (c16 394 vs 390, c32 733 vs 716) and scales to c64=1265 decode
# tok/s (per-user 19), 64/64 ok, ZERO KV-starvation — the fat pool bought nothing (turboquant/int4-KV moot:
# the GDN state dominates, attn-KV is fp8 rounding-error; vllm inflates the attn block to 896 tok to match
# ONE mamba page). dynamic_shapes DEFAULT here (concurrency-robust). SS-latency profile = qwen36-27b-dynshapes
# (VLLM_T_COMPILE_DYNAMIC_SHAPES=false -> SS 39.1, +18%, but concurrency-jittery). MTP deferred (vllm-gaudi
# block-table can't hold the GDN-hybrid multi-group spec layout — framework build, see qwen36-27b-mtp.env).
VLLM_ARGS="--quantization fp8 --kv-cache-dtype fp8_inc --tensor-parallel-size 8 --max-model-len 2048 --max-num-seqs 64 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.04 --block-size 128 --async-scheduling --no-enable-prefix-caching --trust-remote-code"
